    "result_text": "The full test suite passes. The project's test suite consists of the `AcceptanceTest` class (the other test files are the abstract `AcceptanceBase` and the `AuditLogCapture` helper), and all tests are green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `locality` derivation following the codebase's established pattern for derived owner fields (like `displayName`, `initials`, `membershipTier`):\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a fixed `CITY_REGION` table (`Sydney\u2192NSW`, `Melbourne\u2192VIC`, `Brisbane\u2192QLD`) and a derived getter `getLocality()` that returns the canonical region for the owner's city, or `\"UNKNOWN\"` when the city isn't in the table.\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Declared a `locality` read-only property on the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field, which MapStruct auto-maps from `Owner.getLocality()` and Jackson serializes as `$.locality` in the `GET /api/owners/{id}` response.\n\nResult: `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`. A known city (Sydney) returns `NSW`; an unlisted city returns `UNKNOWN`.",
